# API / Contract Discipline

Applies when API work is authorized. API versioning strategy remains OPEN until ADR-005 is frozen.

## Required

- Preserve explicit public contracts
- Validate inputs
- Define consistent error behavior
- Respect idempotency semantics for repeatable operations
- Document breaking changes before shipping them
- Avoid leaking internal implementation details
- Keep provider-specific payment concepts behind adapters
- Request correlation / rate-limit headers where appropriate

## OpenAPI

When API implementation is authorized, OpenAPI represents the public contract. Keep it authoritative and current.

## Prohibited without authorization

- Casually renaming public fields or states
- Silently changing error codes / lifecycle enums exposed publicly
- Creating a new public API shape that contradicts Master Spec or a FROZEN ADR
